02:00:11.139 --> 02:00:13.319
Remember I said that options are very similar to lists,

02:00:13.319 --> 02:00:15.760
except they just have one or zero elements.

02:00:15.760 --> 02:00:19.819
So you can imagine that this is more

02:00:19.819 --> 02:00:22.639
of a basic version of a list,

02:00:22.639 --> 02:00:24.439
but it's much smaller because it's just

02:00:24.439 --> 02:00:26.179
potentially one element or none.

02:00:29.139 --> 02:00:34.139
So here's to talk about nested options.

02:00:34.140 --> 02:00:36.119
So here we have a safe divide function.

02:00:36.760 --> 02:00:42.900
So remember, dividing by zero returns, like, I don't remember what it does in Scala.

02:00:43.020 --> 02:00:44.980
I think in Java you might get not a number.

02:00:45.720 --> 02:00:50.060
I think in Scala you might get, let's see, 3 divided by 0.

